int debug_add_breakpoint(int type, const char *pattern,
                         int line, const char *condition);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds a new breakpoint to the debugger\(cqs linked list.
The breakpoint is created with \f[CR]enabled = 1\f[R] and
\f[CR]hit_count = 0\f[R], assigned a unique ID from the monotonically
increasing \f[CR]next_bp_id\f[R] counter, and prepended to the
breakpoint list.
.PP
If this is the first breakpoint (debug mode was not previously active),
\f[CR]debug_add_breakpoint()\f[R] activates debug mode and registers the
\f[CR]pre_command_hook\f[R] so that command execution will be
intercepted.
.PP
